Upstream files
--------------
LICENSE, VERIFIER_PROVENANCE.md, and src/ other than the files listed under
"Perch delta" are upstream's bytes. UPSTREAM.sha256 lists the sha256 of every
upstream file at the commit above (checked against GitHub when recorded).

Cargo.toml differs from upstream in two places, both because the crate is
built here as a path dependency outside its own workspace:

  - `soroban-sdk = { workspace = true }` became the version the upstream
    workspace pins at that commit, `{ version = "27.0.6", default-features =
    false }`;
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table (upstream's test-utils crate and fixtures,
    which are not vendored) was dropped.

Perch delta
-----------
The zero-knowledge flavor, `UltraKeccakZKFlavor`. README.md's first section
documents it function by function, with Barretenberg references. In summary:

  - src/zk.rs           new: the whole ZK verifier (`UltraHonkZkVerifier`);
  - src/lib.rs          +3 lines: `pub mod zk;` (with a comment) and
                        `pub use zk::{UltraHonkZkVerifier, ZK_PROOF_BYTES,
                        ZK_PROOF_FIELDS};`;
  - src/transcript.rs   visibility only, `fn` -> `pub(crate) fn`: push_point,
                        split_challenge, hash_to_fr,
                        generate_relation_parameters_challenges,
                        generate_alpha_challenges, generate_gate_challenges,
                        generate_gemini_r_challenge,
                        generate_shplonk_z_challenge (rustfmt wraps the last
                        two signatures, one parameter per line, because
                        `pub(crate)` pushes them past its width; the repo's
                        `cargo fmt --all --check` covers path dependencies);
  - src/sumcheck.rs     visibility only: check_sum, partially_evaluate_pow;
  - src/utils.rs        visibility only: point_err;
  - src/verifier.rs     visibility only:
                        UltraHonkVerifier::compute_public_input_delta;
  - README.md           the "Perch delta" section, prepended between
                        `<!-- PERCH DELTA BEGIN` and `<!-- PERCH DELTA END -->`.

Why visibility rather than copies: the ZK verifier then runs the audited code
for every step the two flavors share, so the unaudited surface is src/zk.rs
alone.

crates/perch-zk-adapter/tests/vendor.rs enforces all of the above. It
reverses exactly these edits and requires each result to hash to
UPSTREAM.sha256, so no other byte of an upstream file can change unnoticed.
CHECKSUMS.sha256 pins every file as vendored, so the delta itself cannot
drift either.

Updating
--------
Do not edit these files by hand outside the delta above. To move to a new
upstream commit, replace the directory wholesale, re-apply the two Cargo.toml
changes and the perch delta (and re-audit the delta if upstream changed the
reused functions), then regenerate UPSTREAM.sha256 from the new commit and
CHECKSUMS.sha256 from the result, and update this NOTICE and the
reversal in tests/vendor.rs. Then regenerate the circuit artifacts
(`just zk-artifacts`) and re-run the adapter's real-proof tests. If the new
upstream targets a different Barretenberg version, the pinned toolchain in
scripts/zk-toolchain.sh and crates/perch-zk-prover must move with it: proofs
and verification keys from another bb version fail at the pairing check, not
at parse time.
